# Bulk regression case (assistant-written): a C variadic, `printf`, called
# on Apple ARM64, where arguments past `...` go on the stack (design.md §4.19's
# ladder, rung 1). Until 2026-11-10 it was bound at ONE fixed shape,
# `printf(format: cstr lent, value: i64)`, legal under the strict flags and the
# call-shape reader (panel 103 item 5's own condition: clang says *too many
# arguments* only against a non-variadic prototype). Since panel 243's R1
# (defect 2421) a binding declares no parameter past a header's `...`, where
# nothing held `value` to the `long long` `%lld` reads: the program's own
# header defines the door, `print_count`, a function of a new name with a
# fixed prototype that calls `printf` with the literal format, and the group
# binds that. `printf` writes to the same stdout the runtime writes to, so the
# two lines interleave in order.
extern "ffi-variadic-at-a-fixed-arity.h"
    function print_count(n: i64) -> i32

function main()
    _ = print_count(n: 42)
    print(7)
